  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "It is given that one root of \\(2x^2+rx+s=0,\\) with \\(r\\) and \\(s\\) real numbers, is \\(3+2i\\) \\((i=\\sqrt{-1}).\\) The value of \\(s\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "undetermined"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-13\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(26\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "26"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The other root is \\(3-2i.\\) Their product is \\[ (3+2i)(3-2i)=9+4=13. \\] Vieta’s formula gives \\(\\frac{s}{2}=13,\\) so \\(s=26.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "A polynomial with real coefficients also has the conjugate root",
        "Use the product of the roots and Vieta’s formula"
      ],
